  "name": null,
  "problem": "Let $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t)⟩$ be the position vector of the eagle. Find the distance between the eagle and its nest at time $t=5\\,\\text{s},$ rounded to two decimal places.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The eagle is approximately$\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\text{m}$ away from its nest after $t=5$ seconds.",
  "worked_solution": "Since the nest is at the origin, the distance between the bird and its nest at time $t=5$ is $|r(5)|.$\n\nWe know that $y(5)=\\frac{95}{3}.$ Evaluating the function at $t=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(5) & =⟨\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{5}),\\frac{95}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{95}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(5)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}+{(\\frac{95}{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16}+\\frac{9\\,025}{9}} \\\\  & ≈31.68\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places.",
